---
export const title = 'Keyboard and accessibility';
export const order = 300;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  The list has <code>role="list"</code>, named by <code>label</code>, and each rendered item
  <code>role="listitem"</code> with <code>aria-setsize</code> (the full length) and
  <code>aria-posinset</code>, so a screen reader announces "item 4,312 of 10,000" even though only
  a few items exist in the page. An item that has focus stays rendered when it scrolls out of view,
  so focus is never lost to recycling.
</p>
<p>
  By default the list is one scroll container that the keyboard scrolls, and controls inside the
  items keep their own Tab order. Set <code>navigable</code> to make the items themselves one tab
  stop: <kbd>Up</kbd> and <kbd>Down</kbd> move to the previous and next item,
  <kbd>Page Up</kbd> and <kbd>Page Down</kbd> by a view, <kbd>Home</kbd> and <kbd>End</kbd> to the
  first and last of all items, scrolling as needed.
</p>
<p>
  Every item has the same height. Items of different heights are not supported.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-virtual-list
    id='virtual-list-navigable'
    navigable
    label='Countries'
    item-height='40'
    style='width: 100%; max-width: 360px; height: 12rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-outline-variant);'
  ></wc-virtual-list>
  <script is:inline>
    const $countries = document.getElementById('virtual-list-navigable');
    $countries.items = Array.from({ length: 2000 }, (_, index) => `Row ${index + 1}`);
    $countries.renderItem = item => item;
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
